141 - What Child Is This?
 / 
Key: Em
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 141
Topic: Jesus Christ - 

Verse 1:
[Em]What child is this, who, [D]laid to rest, On [Em]Mary's [Am]lap is s[B]leeping?
Whom [Em]angels greet with [D]anthems sweet, While [Em]shepherds [B]watch are [Em]keeping?
[Bm]This, [G]this is [D]Christ the King, Whom [Em]shepherds [Am]guard and [B]angels sing:
[Bm]Haste, [G]haste to [D]bring Him laud, The [Em]babe, the [B]son of [Em]Mary.

Refrain:
[Em]This, [D]this [Em]is [Am]Christ [B]the King,
[Em]Whom [D]shepherds [Em]guard [B]and [Em]angels sing:
[Bm]Haste, [G]haste [D]to [Em]bring [Am]Him [B]laud,
[Bm]The [G]babe, [D]the [Em]son [B]of [Em]Mary.

Verse 2:
[Em]Why [D]lies [Em]He in [Am]such [B]mean estate
[Em]Where [D]ox [Em]and [B]ass [Em]are feeding?
[Bm]Good [G]Christian, [D]fear: [Em]for [Am]sinners [B]here
[Bm][G]The [D]silent [Em]Word [B]is [Em]pleading.

Verse 3:
[Em]So [D]bring [Em]Him incense, [Am]gold, [B]and myrrh,
[Em]Come, [D]peasant, [Em]king, [B]to [Em]own Him,
[Bm]The [G]King [D]of [Em]kings [Am]salvation [B]brings,
[Bm][G]Let [D]loving [Em]hearts [B]enthrone [Em]Him.
